THIS IS THE RACE CONDITION: lines #2, #4 and #6 show Worker-1, Worker-2
and Worker-3 all reading Resource 10 as AVAILABLE before any of them had
written a result back (the first "reserved by" line is #7, after all
three checks already happened). Because the check-then-write sequence
isn't protected by a lock, all three requests that arrived first at each
idle worker were told SUCCESS for the same resource — three different
clients "own" resource 10 at once, which should never happen.
